048 - Softly Now the Light of Day
 / 
Key: Eb
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 48
Topic: Worship - 

Verse 1:
[Eb/Bb]Softly [Fm/C]now [Eb/Bb]the [Am]light [Bb]of day
[Eb/Bb]Fades [Cm]upon [Eb/Bb]out [Ab]sight [Bb7/Ab]away:
[Eb/Bb]Free [Fm/Ab]from care, [Eb/Bb]from [Am]labor [Bb]free,
[Eb/Bb]Lord, [Gb/Db]we [Cm]would commune with [Bb/F]Thee.

Verse 2:
[Eb/Bb]Thou, [Fm/Ab]whose allpervading [Bb]eye
[Eb/Bb]Nought escapes, without, [Bb7/Ab]within,
[Eb/Bb]Pardon [Fm/C]each [Eb/Bb]infirmity,
[Eb/Bb]Open [Cm]fault, and [Ab]secret [Bb/F]sin.

Verse 3:
[Eb/Bb]Soon [Fm/Ab]from us [Eb/Bb]the [Am]light [Bb]of day
[Eb/Bb]Shall [Cm]forever [Ab]pass [Bb7/Ab]away;
[Eb/Bb]Then, [Fm/Ab]from sin [Eb/Bb]and [Am]sorrow [Bb]free,
[Eb/Bb]Take [Gb/Db]us, [Cm]Lord, to [Ab]dwell [Cm/G]with [Bb/F]Thee.
